Kubernetes Pod Deployment - pod-nginx
This README documents the task configuration, deployment steps, and verification process for creating the pod-nginx Kubernetes pod as required by the Nautilus DevOps team.

Task Requirements
Pod Name: pod-nginx

Image: nginx:latest

Label: app=nginx_app

Container Name: nginx-container

Configuration File (pod.yaml)
YAML
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx_app
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nginx-container
    image: nginx:latest
Deployment Steps
Create or update the manifest file on the jump-host:

Bash
cat <<EOF > pod.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx_app
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nginx-container
    image: nginx:latest
EOF
Delete any existing conflicting pod instance and apply the new configuration:

Bash
kubectl delete pod pod-nginx --ignore-not-found=true
kubectl apply -f pod.yaml
Verification and Previews
1. Check Pod Status and Details
Run the following command to verify that the pod is running and properly scheduled:

Bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx -o wide
Expected Preview Output:

Plaintext
NAME        READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE   IP           NODE        NOMINATED NODE   READINESS GATES
pod-nginx   1/1     Running   0          5s    10.22.0.10   jump-host   <none>           <none>
2. Verify Exact Specifications (Labels, Container Name, Image)
Run the following custom JSONPath query to confirm all parameters match the task criteria precisely:

Bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx -o jsonpath='{"Pod Name: "}{.metadata.name}{"\n"}{"Labels: "}{.metadata.labels}{"\n"}{"Container Name: "}{.spec.containers[0].name}{"\n"}{"Image: "}{.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
Expected Preview Output:

Plaintext
Pod Name: pod-nginx
Labels: {"app":"nginx_app"}
Container Name: nginx-container
Image: nginx:latest
